  (set iteration 0)
  (set max-iterations 100)
  
  (while (< iteration max-iterations)
    ;; Generate response (streaming happens implicitly)
    (set response (generate dialog model 
                           :tools tools
                           :server-tools server-tools
                           :thinking-budget thinking-budget))
    
    (if (tool-calls? response)
        (progn
          ;; Execute tools, get results
          (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response)))
          ;; Append results to dialog
          (set dialog (append dialog response tool-results))
          (set iteration (+ iteration 1)))
      
      ;; No tools - append response and we're done
      (progn
        (set dialog (append dialog response))
        (return dialog)))))
```

This is cleaner - the agent works with dialog as the main data structure. The runtime handles where/how to render things (could be a buffer, could be a web UI, could be just stored in memory).

