# ASSISTANT

# Agent DSL Specification (Updated)

## Agent Communication & Control

### Message Passing
```elisp
(send agent message)
;; Send message to agent's inbox, non-blocking

(receive)
;; Block until message arrives, returns message

(try-receive)
;; Non-blocking check, returns message or nil

(has-messages?)
;; Check if inbox has messages
```

### Interruption & Signaling
```elisp
(interrupt agent signal)
;; Send interrupt signal to agent

(check-interrupted?)
;; Check if this agent has been interrupted, returns signal or nil

(pause agent)
;; Pause agent execution

(resume agent)
;; Resume paused agent

(cancel agent)
;; Terminate agent
```

### Shared State
```elisp
(set-shared key value)
;; Set shared state visible to all agents

(get-shared key)
;; Read shared state

(update-shared key fn)
;; Atomically update shared state with function
```

---

## Updated Examples

### 2. Reflection Agent (Every N Messages - Updated)

```elisp
(def-agent reflective (dialog model tools server-tools)
  (set primary-model 'claude-sonnet-4-5)
  (set reflection-model 'gpt-5)
  (set reflection-frequency 10)  ;; Every 10 messages
  
  (while true
    ;; Reflect when dialog length is multiple of frequency
    (when (= 0 (mod (length dialog) reflection-frequency))
      (set reflection-prompt '(((role . "user")
                                (content . "Review current status and course correct if needed."))))
      (set reflection (generate (append dialog reflection-prompt) 
                               reflection-model
                               :tools nil
                               :stream false))
      (set dialog (append dialog reflection-prompt reflection)))
    
    (set response (generate dialog primary-model
                           :tools tools
                           :stream true))
    
    (if (tool-calls? response)
        (progn
          (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream true))
          (set dialog (append dialog response tool-results)))
      (progn
        (set dialog (append dialog response))
        (return dialog)))))
```

### 9. Monitored Agent (Supervisor Can Interrupt)

```elisp
(def-agent monitored (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Agent that can be interrupted and redirected by supervisor"
  
  (while true
    ;; Check for interrupts before each generation
    (set interrupt-signal (check-interrupted?))
    (if interrupt-signal
        (progn
          (set new-instruction (get interrupt-signal 'instruction))
          (set dialog (append dialog 
                            (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                                       (cons 'content new-instruction))))))
      nil)
    
    (set response (generate dialog model
                           :tools tools
                           :stream true))
    
    (if (tool-calls? response)
        (progn
          (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream true))
          (set dialog (append dialog response tool-results)))
      (progn
        (set dialog (append dialog response))
        (return dialog)))))

(def-agent supervisor (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Spawns worker and monitors progress, can interrupt"
  
  ;; Spawn the monitored worker
  (set worker (new-agent monitored dialog model tools server-tools))
  
  (while (running? worker)
    ;; Every 5 messages, check worker's progress
    (when (= 0 (mod (length (get-shared "worker-dialog")) 5))
      (set worker-dialog (get-shared "worker-dialog"))
      (set review-prompt
           (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                      (cons 'content 
                            (format "Review worker progress:\n%s\nShould we redirect?" 
                                   worker-dialog)))))
      (set review (generate review-prompt 'gpt-5
                           :tools nil
                           :stream false))
      
      (if (get review 'should-redirect)
          (interrupt worker 
                    (list (cons 'instruction (get review 'new-direction))))
        nil))
    
    ;; Sleep briefly
    (sleep 1.0))
  
  (set final-dialog (wait worker))
  (return final-dialog))
```

### 10. Collaborative Agents (Message Passing)

```elisp
(def-agent researcher (query partner-agent)
  "Research agent that can ask partner for help"
  
  (set task-dialog (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                              (cons 'content query))))
  
  (while true
    (set response (generate task-dialog 'claude-sonnet-4-5
                           :tools '(read-webpage ripgrep)
                           :stream false))
    
    ;; Check if we need help
    (if (has-key? response 'needs-help)
        (progn
          ;; Ask partner for help
          (send partner-agent (list (cons 'type "help-request")
                                   (cons 'question (get response 'help-question))))
          
          ;; Wait for partner's response
          (set help-response (receive))
          (set task-dialog (append task-dialog response
                                 (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                                            (cons 'content 
                                                  (get help-response 'answer)))))))
      
      ;; Check if partner needs our help
      (set incoming (try-receive))
      (if (and incoming (= (get incoming 'type) "help-request"))
          (progn
            ;; Answer partner's question
            (set help-dialog (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                                        (cons 'content (get incoming 'question)))))
            (set help-answer (generate help-dialog 'claude-opus-4
                                     :tools nil
                                     :stream false))
            (send partner-agent (list (cons 'type "help-response")
                                     (cons 'answer help-answer)))
            ;; Continue our work
            (if (tool-calls? response)
                (progn
                  (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream false))
                  (set task-dialog (append task-dialog response tool-results)))
              (return task-dialog)))
        
        ;; No help needed either way
        (if (tool-calls? response)
            (progn
              (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream false))
              (set task-dialog (append task-dialog response tool-results)))
          (return task-dialog))))))

(def-agent collaborative-research (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Spawn two researchers that can help each other"
  
  (set response (generate dialog model :stream true))
  (set queries (get response 'research-queries))
  
  ;; Spawn two researchers
  (set researcher-a (new-agent researcher (nth 0 queries) nil))
  (set researcher-b (new-agent researcher (nth 1 queries) nil))
  
  ;; Connect them to each other (pass handles after creation)
  (send researcher-a (list (cons 'partner researcher-b)))
  (send researcher-b (list (cons 'partner researcher-a)))
  
  ;; Wait for both to complete
  (set results (wait-all (list researcher-a researcher-b)))
  
  ;; Synthesize results
  (set synthesis-prompt
       (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                  (cons 'content 
                        (format "Synthesize these research results:\n%s" results)))))
  (set synthesis (generate synthesis-prompt model :stream true))
  
  (return (append dialog synthesis-prompt synthesis)))
```

### 11. Interrupt-Driven Agent (React to External Events)

```elisp
(def-agent interrupt-driven (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Agent that processes interrupts as high-priority tasks"
  
  (set main-task-active true)
  
  (while main-task-active
    ;; Check for interrupts first
    (set interrupt-signal (check-interrupted?))
    (if interrupt-signal
        (progn
          ;; Handle interrupt immediately
          (set interrupt-prompt
               (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                          (cons 'content 
                                (format "URGENT: %s" (get interrupt-signal 'message))))))
          (set interrupt-response (generate (append dialog interrupt-prompt)
                                          model
                                          :tools tools
                                          :stream true))
          (set dialog (append dialog interrupt-prompt interrupt-response))
          
          ;; Resume main task
          (set resume-prompt
               (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                          (cons 'content "Resume the original task."))))
          (set dialog (append dialog resume-prompt)))
      nil)
    
    ;; Continue main task
    (set response (generate dialog model
                           :tools tools
                           :stream true))
    
    (if (tool-calls? response)
        (progn
          (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream true))
          (set dialog (append dialog response tool-results)))
      (progn
        (set dialog (append dialog response))
        (set main-task-active false))))
  
  (return dialog))
```

### 12. Tournament Agent (Multiple Attempts, Best Wins)

```elisp
(def-agent tournament (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Spawn multiple agents with different strategies, judge winner"
  
  (def-agent contestant (strategy-dialog contestant-model)
    (set iteration 0)
    (while (< iteration 10)
      ;; Check if tournament is over
      (if (get-shared "tournament-complete")
          (return strategy-dialog)
        nil)
      
      (set response (generate strategy-dialog contestant-model
                             :tools tools
                             :stream false))
      (if (tool-calls? response)
          (progn
            (set results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream false))
            (set strategy-dialog (append strategy-dialog response results))
            (set iteration (+ iteration 1)))
        (return strategy-dialog))))
  
  ;; Spawn contestants with different models
  (set models '(claude-opus-4 gpt-5 gemini-2-5-pro))
  (set contestants
       (map (lambda (m) (new-agent contestant dialog m))
            models))
  
  ;; Set up shared state
  (set-shared "tournament-complete" false)
  
  ;; Wait for all to complete or timeout after 60 seconds
  (set results (wait-all contestants))
  (set-shared "tournament-complete" true)
  
  ;; Judge which result is best
  (set judge-prompt
       (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                  (cons 'content 
                        (format "Judge these 3 solutions and pick the best:\n%s" results)))))
  (set judgment (generate judge-prompt 'gpt-5
                         :tools nil
                         :stream false))
  (set winner-idx (get judgment 'best-index))
  (set winner-dialog (nth winner-idx results))
  
  ;; Stream winner's dialog to UI
  (return winner-dialog))
```

### 13. Delegating Agent with Status Updates

```elisp
(def-agent delegating (dialog model tools server-tools)
  "Delegate subtasks and receive status updates"
  
  (def-agent worker (task-description manager-agent)
    (set task-dialog (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                                (cons 'content task-description))))
    (set steps 0)
    
    (while (< steps 20)
      (set response (generate task-dialog 'claude-sonnet-4-5
                             :tools tools
                             :stream false))
      
      ;; Send status update to manager
      (send manager-agent 
            (list (cons 'type "status-update")
                 (cons 'task task-description)
                 (cons 'progress (format "Step %d: %s" steps response))))
      
      (if (tool-calls? response)
          (progn
            (set tool-results (execute-tools (tool-calls response) :stream false))
            (set task-dialog (append task-dialog response tool-results))
            (set steps (+ steps 1)))
        (progn
          ;; Task complete
          (send manager-agent
                (list (cons 'type "task-complete")
                     (cons 'task task-description)
                     (cons 'result task-dialog)))
          (return task-dialog)))))
  
  ;; Get initial plan
  (set response (generate dialog model :stream true))
  (set subtasks (get response 'subtasks))
  
  ;; Spawn workers for each subtask
  (set self-handle (get-shared "current-agent"))
  (set workers
       (map (lambda (task) (new-agent worker task self-handle))
            subtasks))
  
  ;; Monitor workers and provide updates
  (set completed 0)
  (set total (length workers))
  
  (while (< completed total)
    (set msg (receive))
    (if (= (get msg 'type) "status-update")
        (progn
          ;; Log status
          (set dialog (append dialog
                            (list (list (cons 'role "assistant")
                                       (cons 'content (get msg 'progress)))))))
      
      (if (= (get msg 'type) "task-complete")
          (set completed (+ completed 1))
        nil)))
  
  ;; All workers done, synthesize
  (set results (wait-all workers))
  (set synthesis-prompt
       (list (list (cons 'role "user")
                  (cons 'content (format "Synthesize:\n%s" results)))))
  (set synthesis (generate synthesis-prompt model :stream true))
  
  (return (append dialog synthesis-prompt synthesis)))
```

---

## Key Communication Patterns

1. **Interruption**: Supervisor can redirect worker mid-execution
2. **Message Passing**: Peers collaborate by sending messages
3. **Shared State**: All agents can read/write common state
4. **Status Updates**: Workers report progress to manager
5. **Tournament**: Multiple agents compete, winner selected
6. **Priority Handling**: Interrupts pause main task, resume after

The runtime must provide:
- Message queues per agent
- Interrupt signal delivery
- Thread-safe shared state
- Agent handle management

